  "repo_truth": "Review the exact 47-file working-tree subject against reviewed baseline commit 5cf41d2f64d68cb7f78abb5eccab9acf307089d3. The subject contains no production/library file. Its three Rust files are CLI integration tests; remaining files are exact fixture authority inputs, generated proof bytes, selector/dispatch lineage, and slice-local specification/plan/proof records. Parent command evidence to verify independently: complete P3/P3B packet wall 273 tests with no failure; cargo test --workspace --quiet exit 0 after 812 seconds with two platform-marked ignores; cargo fmt --all -- --check exit 0; strict clippy for pipeline/compiler/cli all targets exit 0; archive boundary normal/self-test exit 0; git diff --check exit 0. Four named transient post-capture outputs are absent. Eight unrelated pre-existing .claude/**, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md paths are outside the subject. No classification or proof-level promotion is requested in P3B.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Replay all 47 manifest hashes and compare the complete subject with baseline 5cf41d2f64d68cb7f78abb5eccab9acf307089d3.",
    "Review the three test deltas, fixture-authority mirrors, profile inputs, rich Work Specification identity, canonical-YAML consumers, generated views, transcript/scorecard/plan bytes, and paired compile goldens.",
    "Trace real Stage 10 preview/apply, canonical YAML persistence, generated Markdown view, handoff identity, and M5 planning consumption through the named tests and existing production call paths.",
    "Verify every selector and immutable dispatch stays within P3B, that transient generated outputs and repository identity are absent, and that no sibling seam or production symbol changed.",
    "Verify the reported targeted, negative, workspace, lint, archive, and diff proof from live repository truth as needed.",
    "Identify findings independently before comparing only P3/P4 candidates with the selected-scope entries in 09."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, formatting, staging, commit, push, handoff, ledger, dispatch, or delegation.",
    "No P1A, P1B, P1C, P2, P4, P5, P6, P7, sibling-slice, production/runtime, schema/definition, public API, dependency, Cargo/version, unsafe-policy, release, or migration work.",
    "No classification or proof-level promotion; P3B may prove only CLI/test integration of the already-reviewed P3 Work Specification boundary.",
    "Do not accept generated Markdown as canonical authority, committed fixture identity, committed post-capture output, dynamic schema inference, or changes to any indeterminate refusal."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Verify complete subject identity, whitespace hygiene, exact baseline diff, and the absence of out-of-scope or generated debris.",
    "Review correctness of the three CLI test changes and trace their affected real call paths without relying on parent implementation rationale.",
    "Validate the ten fixture-authority inputs, pairwise mirror equality, rich M4 canonical input/feature identity, canonical M5 consumer, deterministic views/evidence, and both shared compile goldens.",
    "Validate positive, negative, fail-closed, real-path, workspace, lint, archive, and diff proof; report any missing or misleading evidence.",
    "Check selector/dispatch/proof lineage, reviewability, sibling non-widening, and the zero-promotion ceiling.",
    "Return findings first in Critical, Required, Optional, Nit order with severity, file and line, violated contract/invariant/gate, why wrong, smallest valid remediation, and missing verification."
  ],
  "contracts_and_gates": [
    "Canonical Stage 10 authority is artifacts/work-specification/work-specification.yaml; artifacts/feature_spec/FEATURE_SPEC.md is generated and non-authoritative",
    "All supported intake/validation paths retain the exact released Work Specification schema and every other fail-closed refusal",
    "Fresh test repositories use setup-owned identity without committing identity bytes",
    "Foundation happy/skip paths preserve feature identity fs-m4-foundation-journey-2026-04 and consume canonical YAML for M5 planning",
    "Fixture authority mirrors and profile inputs are pairwise byte-identical; generated post-capture outputs remain absent",
    "Shared compile goldens are deterministic across all eleven CLI/compiler/pipeline consumers",
    "No production symbol, released schema/definition, public API, Cargo/dependency, sibling seam, classification, or proof-level change is permitted",
    "No unresolved valid P1/P2 may remain before commit"
  ],
  "stop_conditions": [
    "Return blocked if complete subject identity, baseline diff, or required read-only evidence cannot be established.",
    "Report rather than repair any finding.",
    "Do not edit, delegate, create another dispatch, write a handoff, modify the ledger, stage, commit, or push."
  ],
